Relay patch for Zig 0.17.0's standard library: std.Io.Threaded on iOS.

Io.Threaded.NullFile has no `fd` on iOS, yet spawnDarwin (which iOS
compiles too, via the Threaded vtable) reads it, so any iOS build
that uses Io.Threaded fails to compile. libghostty does
(src/global.zig). Zig's master branch fixed it the same way: iOS gets
the POSIX NullFile. Drop this patch once the Zig pin includes the fix.

Applied by Scripts/build-libghostty.sh to the toolchain it fetches.

--- a/lib/std/Io/Threaded.zig
+++ b/lib/std/Io/Threaded.zig
@@ -354,7 +354,7 @@
             }
         }
     },
-    .wasi, .ios, .tvos, .visionos, .watchos => struct {
+    .wasi, .tvos, .visionos, .watchos => struct {
         fn deinit(this: @This()) void {
             _ = this;
         }
